{{zh-forms|alt=匹}}
A {{w|Mainland Southeast Asia linguistic area|Southeast Asian areal etymon}} (STEDT). Compare:
* Tai-Kadai: {{cog|tai-pro|*pitᴰ||duck}} > {{cog|th|เป็ด}}, {{cog|lo|ເປັດ}}, {{cog|za|bit}};
* Austroasiatic: {{cog|mkh-vie-pro|*viːt||duck}} > {{cog|vi|vịt}}, to which ([http://pacling.anu.edu.au/series/SEALS-PDFs/alves2015etyma.pdf Alves 2015]) proposes a Tai origin;
* Sino-Tibetan:
** {{cog|mxj|kɹɑi³⁵ pit⁵⁵|kɹɑi³⁵ '''pit⁵⁵'''|duck}};
** {{cog|bxd|pjɛ̱t⁵⁵||duck}}, {{cog|atb|pje̱t⁵⁵||duck}};
** {{cog|tbq-lob-pro|*baj¹/²|t=duck}} > {{cog|my|ဘဲ}}.

Now considered obsolete in Sinitic and Sino-Xenic; the common word for "duck" in modern Sinitic is {{och-l|鴨|}}.

