===Etymology 1===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|かも|alt=鳧}}
{{swp|ja:カモ}}
{{swp|Duck}}
[[File:Anas_crecca_landing_on_the_water.JPG|thumb|250px|{{lang|ja|鴨}} (''kamo''): a pair of '''[[duck]]s'''.]]

{{unk|ja|sort=かも}}. Possibly a shift or alteration of {{inh|ja|ojp|sort=かも|-}} {{ja-r|浮かむ|うかむ|to [[float]]}}, modern {{ja-r|浮かぶ|うかぶ}}. Alternatively, may derive from {{der|ja|ltc|sort=かも|-}} {{ltc-l|雁|a type of wild goose}}, borrowed with the {{ja-glossary|kan'on}} reading ''gan'', with initial ''g'' changing to ''k'' due to the avoidance of voiced stops at the start of Japanese words in older times, and final ''n'' changing to ''mu'' due to apparent lack of final ''n'' in {{cog|ojp|-}}. also may be cognate with Old Chinese 鴨 (OC: *qraːb, MC: *ʔap).

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|かも|acc=1|acc_ref=NHK,DJR}}

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|かも|カモ}}

# a [[duck]]
# {{lb|ja|sort=かも|slang}} {{qualifier|from the way ducks return to the same place and are thus easy to hunt}} a [[mark]] or easy [[target]] for a [[swindle]], someone who is likely to lose at [[gambling]] or other competition
# {{lb|ja|sort=かも|slang}} {{qualifier|from the good flavor of duck meat}} short for {{ja-r|鴨の味|かも の あじ|duck [[flavor]]}}: a very good [[flavor]]; by extension, any remarkably good [[sensation]] or [[feeling]], particularly describing happy [[married]] [[life]]
# {{lb|ja|sort=かも|slang}} {{qualifier|from the uniform of black clothing}} short for {{ja-r|黒%鴨|くろ%がも|[[black]] duck}}: a [[male]] [[servant]], such as a [[butler]] or [[chauffeur]] (compare English {{m|en|penguin}})

